 Day 9 — GCP Monitoring + Logging + Alerting (Cloud Ops Suite)

Scenario-Based DevOps real Interview Questions

1️⃣ Your production service experiences random latency spikes. How will you design proactive monitoring using SLOs, SLIs, and alert policies?

2️⃣ Logs from multiple GKE clusters and services are scattered. How will you centralize, structure, and route logs for analysis?

3️⃣ You need real-time alerts only when error rate breaches a threshold for 5 minutes, not on single spikes. How will you configure the alerting condition?

4️⃣ A team wants to filter logs generated only by specific microservices and export them to BigQuery. How will you design log-based routing?

5️⃣ Your application crashed but logs were missing. How will you guarantee delivery and retention of logs for critical systems?

6️⃣ You need to identify which user or service account deleted a VM or changed firewall rules. Where and how will you investigate?

7️⃣ Alerts are firing too frequently causing alert fatigue. What steps will you take to refine policies and reduce noise?

8️⃣ A developer needs access to logs of only two services without seeing logs of other environments. How will you design IAM + log views?

9️⃣ Your SRE team wants dashboards showing CPU, latency, error rate, memory, traffic, and cost. How will you design a unified monitoring dashboard?

🔟 You need anomaly detection (AI/ML-based) for production metrics. Which Cloud Monitoring features will you enable and why?

1️⃣1️⃣ Logs ingestion cost is increasing rapidly. What optimizations can you apply without losing observability?

1️⃣2️⃣ You need to track API usage, IAM changes, security events, and admin actions. Which logs will you enable and where will you store them?

1️⃣3️⃣ A service running on Cloud Run must send structured logs with trace correlation. How will you implement this?

1️⃣4️⃣ You want distributed tracing across microservices deployed on GKE + Cloud Run. Which GCP tools will you use and how will you integrate them?

1️⃣5️⃣ You need uptime checks for both internal and external services. How will you configure them with appropriate alerting and failure thresholds?

